#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lambdachat: serve a Hugging Face model with vLLM on a Lambda Cloud GPU box and chat with it from this machine.

  lambdachat up                 launch a box (cheapest that fits) and serve the model; reuses a running box
  lambdachat ui                 Open WebUI in the browser (local, http://localhost:13000); runs `up` first if needed
  lambdachat chat               terminal chat; every conversation is saved as JSON
  lambdachat api [--env]        open the tunnel and print the OpenAI-compatible endpoint for scripts and eval harnesses
  lambdachat status             box, model, cost so far, idle timer, tunnel and UI
  lambdachat keepalive on|off   pause or resume the box's idle auto-terminate
  lambdachat logs               follow the vLLM log on the box
  lambdachat ssh [cmd...]       shell on the box
  lambdachat down               terminate the box and stop the tunnel and local UI
  lambdachat adopt ID           manage an instance launched some other way (then run `lambdachat up` to provision it)

Settings live in config.env next to this script; override them in ~/.config/lambda-vllm-chat/config.env or with
LAMBDACHAT_<KEY>=value. The Lambda API key comes from $LAMBDA_API_KEY or ~/.config/lambda/api-key.
"""

